  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The write and its queue commit together",
      "items": [
        "the optimistic row and the queued mutation land in one SQLite transaction — no half-written local state, no dual-write gap",
        "the local store is a projection, not authority: the server refresh replaces it and the server resolves the conflict",
        "the outbox is persisted, so it survives a crash, a quit and a laptop lid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The drain is not the GUI thread",
      "items": [
        "drains fire on startup, on reconnect and on a timer; the work itself runs on a worker thread — never a blocking call on the GUI thread",
        "every send carries an idempotency key, so a retried request is applied once",
        "the retry ladder is bounded and ends in a dead-letter view for admins, not in an infinite loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Failure is visible",
      "items": [
        "on failure the previous value is restored and the reason is shown — an error is a value, and it never crosses a layer as an exception",
        "the ViewModel maps the outcome onto one closed status enum: Ready, Empty, Forbidden, NotFound, Offline, Error or PolicyBlocked",
        "the SDK owns QNetworkAccessManager; the reply is aborted when a newer request supersedes it, and the stale result is dropped"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
